The '''Protocol for the Greenification of Baliscan Society''' ({{lang-bl|Protocolo Ecologización Sociedad Baliscana}}), popularly known as the '''Green Protocol''' ({{lang-bl|Protocolo verde}}) is a set of policy initiatives by the [[Confederal Congress]] with the overarching aim of making Balisca [[W:Climate neutral|climate neutral]] by 2032. An impact assessed plan was developed between 1982 and and 2002, in order to determine how to achieve [[Climate change in Balisca#Greenhouse gases emissions|confederal greenhouse gas emission]] reductions target for 2030 to at least 50% and towards 60% compared with 1990 levels. The protocol is to review each existing law on its climate merits, and also introduce new legislation on [[W:Doughnut (economic model)|doughnut economics]], the [[w:Circular economy|circular economy]], {{W|building renovation}}, {{W|restoration ecology}}, {{W|rewilding|restoring}} and protecting [[w:Biodiversity|biodiversity]], expanding {{W|aquaculture}} and encouraging [[w:Innovation|innovation]].

Shortly after the discovery of the {{W|Ozone depletion|hole in the ozone layer}} above {{W|Antarctica}} in 1982, Balisca became the first country to declare a [[w:Climate emergency declaration|climate emergency]]. The administration passed legislation committing the Baliscan government to introduce measures to reduce CO2 emission below their 1990 levels, facilitate the development of {{W|green technology}}, and eliminate dependence on {{W|fossil fuels}}. Additionally, the Protocol advocated for the adoption of {{W|bioregionalism}}, {{W|decentralization}} and {{W|localism}}. Subsequent governments embraced the adoption of new technology in combination with Indigenous land management and farming practice, such as {{W|Chinampa|chinampa}}, {{W|terrace farming}} and {{W|controlled forest burning}}. Balisca fully {{W|fossil fuel divestment|divested from fossil fuels}} in 2015, becoming the first country to do so.

In response to the economic slowdown caused by the [[w:COVID-19 pandemic|COVID-19 pandemic]], the Baliscan electorate (by wide margins) supported stronger initiatives aimed at encouraging [[w:Green recovery|green recovery]] and accelerating [[W:Climate change mitigation|decarbonization]]. These initiatives were later expanded into their own standalone policy following much congressional debate. In total, the Green Protocol was allocated an unprecedented $207 billion towards sustainable development (including renewable energy sources, eco-communities, and research into new environmental technology), and another pledged $1.1 trillion in funding through 2050.

== Goals ==
# [[W:Emissions reduction|Reducing emissions]] to stay under 1.5&nbsp;°C of warming.
# Transferring/protecting millions of high-wage [[W:Trade union|union]] position and ensuring [[W:Economic security|economic security]] and a [[W:Just transition|just transition]].
# Investments in [[W:Infrastructure|infrastructure]] and [[W:Clean industry|cleantech]].
# Ensuring [[W:Water pollution|clean water]], [[W:Air pollution|clean air]], [[W:Climate resilience|climate resilience]], [[W:Healthy diet|healthy food]], the ability to access nature, and sustainable environment.
# Promoting justice and promoting equality.

